{
  "version": 1,
  "snapshot": "test/fixtures/dom-snapshot.html",
  "notes": [
    "Every anchor the skin's CSS is allowed to depend on. The contract test asserts each 'boot' anchor appears in the snapshot, and lints css/*.css so no rule targets an anchor that is missing here.",
    "tier=boot: rendered on a fresh, unsigned-in profile (captured by scripts/capture-snapshot.mjs).",
    "tier=session: needs an open session on a signed-in profile; reported as pending until such a snapshot exists.",
    "tier=flow: needs at least one message turn; same pending treatment.",
    "M1 note: the transcript-side anchors (class.bubble / class.column / class.slot / flow.*) are still pending a real session, but their rules are checked separately by scripts/check-messages.mjs against test/fixtures/messages.html, which reproduces the host's message DOM (real class suffixes + data attributes, reduced host base CSS).",
    "M1 note: attr.body.dark (data-ds-dark-theme on <body>) is written by ui-layout's theme presenter only in dark mode; scripts/screenshots.mjs emulates prefers-color-scheme: dark and asserts the attribute before saving m1-dark-new.png.",
    "M2 note: attr.body.mode (data-chatgpt-mode) is written by this skin's own switcher for display rules only — permissions come from lib/host/chat-policy.js, never from the attribute. It is session tier because a fresh page has no conversation to describe.",
    "M2 note: the hero mode cards and the header.leading product segment are asserted live on the sessionless page too (hero.options is behind `sessionId !== undefined`), so class.chatgptModeCard / class.chatgptModeSwitch stay session tier; scripts/screenshots.mjs asserts them live against a blank session.",
    "M3 note: in Chat mode the Host permission chip ([data-slot='conversation.input.permission']) is hidden because it names a Host preset the policy overwrites; the skin's own read-only note (conversation.input.left) states what applies. Hiding a label never changes access — lib/host/chat-policy.js does.",
    "0.2.2 note: the user bubble lost the Sixlwa module class and now carries data-message-bubble from the primitives UserMessageBubble; css/30-chat.css matches both spellings. class.bubble already covers the new `_bubble_` suffix."
  ],
